(function(){var C=window.__CLIPS||(window.__CLIPS={});var d={"Press Begin when you are ready.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Worked example.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Yes.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not quite yet. Have another look, or use a hint.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not quite yet. That's fine. You can try again, or move on without an answer.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Choose an answer first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Type your answer first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Put all of them in order first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Sort all of them first.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You explored new possibilities.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "New idea explored.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You worked through something difficult.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Challenge explored.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You stayed with the challenge.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Strong persistence.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You tried a different approach when your first idea did not work.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "New strategy discovered.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You kept trying.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Learning continued.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "You looked carefully before deciding.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Careful observation.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Folktale: Why Hare Has Long Ears.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Today I am practising understanding a story and the words that build it.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What is a folktale?.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A folktale is an old story that people told aloud. Folktales often explain why something is the way it is, and they teach a lesson.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Read the story.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Read the story. You can press Read aloud to listen to it.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Nouns and adjectives.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A noun names a person, animal, place or thing. A proper noun names a particular one and starts with a capital letter. An adjective describes a noun.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Find the adjectives: \"Hare woke up wet and cold.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "An adjective describes a noun.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Which words tell us what Hare was like?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "\"Wet\" and \"cold\" describe Hare, so they are adjectives.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Who warned the animals about the flood?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Grandmother Tortoise": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Mouse": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Hare": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "The birds": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Look near the start of the story.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Find who \"called all the animals together\".": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "It was the oldest, slowest animal.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Grandmother Tortoise warned them that the river would flood.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What was Hare doing while the others listened?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Racing his shadow": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Sleeping": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Eating grass": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Swimming": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Find the sentence that starts \"All the animals listened, except Hare.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Read the next sentence.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He was busy with a game on the veld.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Hare was racing his own shadow across the veld.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Put the events in the order they happened.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What happens at the very beginning?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "The flood happens at night.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "The ending explains why Hare's ears are long.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Warning, not listening, the flood, then Hare's ears grow long.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Why did Hare say, \"I was foolish\"?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He had not listened to the warning": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He lost a race": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He was hungry": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He did not like rain": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What happened to Hare that night?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Why did he get wet when the others did not?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "He did not move his home because he did not listen.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Hare got wet and cold because he did not listen to Tortoise's warning.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What lesson does this folktale teach?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "It is wise to listen": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Running fast is the most important thing": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Rivers are always dangerous": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Tortoises are slow": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Think about what Hare learnt.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "What did Tortoise tell Hare to do?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "\"Stretch your ears towards wise words.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "The story teaches that it is wise to listen, especially to good advice.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Sort the words into nouns and adjectives.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A noun is a thing. An adjective describes a thing.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Can you put \"the\" in front of it? Then it is probably a noun.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "short, cold and wise describe things.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "river, ears and rocks are nouns. short, cold and wise are adjectives.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Which word is a proper noun in this story?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Tortoise": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "river": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "rocks": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "wind": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "A proper noun names a particular character.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "It starts with a capital letter in the story.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Look for a character's name.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "\"Tortoise\" is used as a character's name, so it is a proper noun with a capital letter.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "How did you understand the story best?": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Reading it myself": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Listening to it": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Looking back at the text": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Not sure": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Folktales carry wisdom from one generation to the next.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Why Hare Has Long Ears (a 2to.iQ folktale)": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Long ago, Hare had short, round ears, just like Mouse. Hare was quick, but he never listened.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "One afternoon, Grandmother Tortoise called all the animals together. \"Tonight the rain will be heavy,\" she said slowly. \"The river will flood. Move your homes to the high rocks.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "All the animals listened, except Hare. He was busy racing his own shadow across the veld.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "That night, the water rose higher and higher. Hare woke up wet and cold, and he had to swim all the way to the high rocks.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "In the morning, Hare sat shivering beside Tortoise. \"I was foolish,\" he said. \"I wish I could hear better.\"": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Tortoise smiled. \"Then stretch your ears towards wise words,\" she said.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "So every day, Hare stretched his ears to listen to the wind, the birds and his friends. His ears grew longer and longer. And that is why, to this day, Hare has long ears and hears danger before anyone else.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Folktale. an old story passed on by telling it.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Flood. when water covers land that is usually dry.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Veld. open grassland.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "Foolish. not wise.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "\"racing his own shadow\" means running around playing by himself.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,", "\"stretch your ears towards wise words\" means listen carefully to good advice.": "data:audio/mpeg;base64,"};for(var k in d)C[k]=d[k];})();
